\begin{cases} a + 2d = 17 \\ a + 4d = 39 \end{cases}
\] Subtracting the first equation from the second, we get \(2d = 22\), so \(d = 11\). Substituting \(d = 11\) into the first equation, we get \(a + 2 \cdot 11 = 17\), so \(a = 17 - 22 = -5\). The 7th term is \(a_7 = a + 6d = -5 + 6 \cdot 11 = -5 + 66 = 61\). </think> <answer> 61 </answer>

